@startuml

salt
{
  <b>ORE STUDIO - REPORTING: THE MARKET A REPORT PRICES FROM</b>
  Home > Reporting > Run settings > Acme official EOD run settings > Market bindings
  --
  <b>MARKET BINDINGS</b> | Editable | version 7
  It decides which published curve each market role prices from. It does not decide
  the valuation date, the curve configuration or the pricing engines.
  Four reports bind this configuration: Group Consolidated Exposure, Board Risk
  Dashboard, Headline Position, NPV. A change here reaches the next run of all four.
  --
  {#
    Role | Published curve | As-of | State | Publisher | Points
    pricing | USD-SOFR-3M / ACME London | 06 Oct 16:00 | Published | a.reyes | 12
    simulation | NO PUBLISHED CURVE BOUND | - | - | - | -
  }
  Writes, derived and never typed: Markets parameter pricing = USD-SOFR-3M.ACME-London.
  A role with no set bound refuses the run before it starts. It does not price
  from whatever the export happens to find.
  --
  <b>THE PICKER: THE PUBLISHED SETS (RECORD PICKER)</b>
  [ search the curve or the party ] [ Party: ACME London v ] [ ] Show candidates [ ] Show ended sets
  {#
    Curve | Party | As-of | State | Publisher | Points
    USD-SOFR-3M | ACME London | 06 Oct 16:00 | Published | a.reyes | 12
    USD-SOFR-3M | ACME London | 05 Oct 16:00 | Superseded | a.reyes | 12
    EUR-ESTR-6M | ACME London | 06 Oct 16:00 | Published | j.silva | 9
    USD-SOFR-3M | ACME London | 07 Oct 08:10 | Candidate | - | 12
    GBP-SONIA-3M | ACME London | 03 Oct 16:00 | Withdrawn | j.silva | 8
  }
  --
  <b>THE REFUSALS, IN THE DIALOG'S FOOTER</b>
  <color:#ef4444>A CANDIDATE IS REFUSED.</color> That set is a candidate. Nobody has approved it,
  so a run cannot price from it. Ask for the publish to be approved, or pick the published set.
  <color:#ef4444>AN ENDED SET IS REFUSED.</color> That set ended on 06 Oct 16:41Z, superseded by the set
  published at 06 Oct 16:00Z. A run prices from it only when the binding names its as-of.
  [x] Price from this set at its as-of 05 Oct 16:00Z   <- the only route past the refusal
  The binding then names a historical as-of, and every run of this configuration prices
  from that set at that instant until somebody changes it.
  --
  <b>THE RUN: REFUSED, AND THE RUN THAT PRICED</b>
  {#
    Run | Market the run resolves | Outcome
    #4821 | pricing: the candidate 8f3c... | REFUSED: not published
    #4822 | pricing: USD-SOFR-3M ended, no as-of | REFUSED: ended
    #4823 | pricing: USD-SOFR-3M, 05 Oct 16:00 | COMPLETED
  }
  The run that completed names the set it priced from: publish record 8f2a...,
  published by a.reyes at 05 Oct 16:40Z, priced at its as-of on purpose.
  A run names the set it used, not the set the configuration names today.
  --
  <b>THE AUDIT</b>
  The configuration's History tab: the role, the set's curve and as-of, the publish_id
  before and after, the account and the reason. The set's record: the reports bound to
  it and the runs that priced from it (NO READ YET).
}

@enduml
